extension: give the extensions of a child their syscall lists

Some kernels (crDroid's 4.14 for sm6150, and the ones of termux/proot#397)
clear the message of the last ptrace event on every ptrace request, so
PTRACE_GETEVENTMSG always reads 0. PRoot detects them and takes the flags
of a PTRACE_EVENT_SECCOMP stop from the lists its filter was built from:
its own and the ones of the stopped tracee's extensions. Only the first
tracee had these lists, as inherit_extensions() didn't hand them on, so
every forked process lost the FILTER_SYSEXIT of the extensions and its
syscalls skipped their exit stage. With -0 that is where getuid(2) and
the like turn into 0: "proot -0 sh -c 'id -u | cat'" printed the real
uid, and pacman-key stopped with "needs to be run as root".

A child's extensions now point at the same lists as its parent's, which
never change after initialization. Nothing else reads them: the filter is
built once, before the first tracee runs, and on kernels that keep the
event message they are not looked up at all.

Upstream fixed this in 4006c630f with a table of the flags (after
5.1.107.102); this patch can go once proot is updated past it.

diff --git a/src/extension/extension.c b/src/extension/extension.c
--- a/src/extension/extension.c
+++ b/src/extension/extension.c
@@ -155,6 +155,8 @@
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		child_extension->filtered_sysnums = parent_extension->filtered_sysnums;
+
 		if (status == 0) {
 			/* ... with a shared config or ...  */
 			child_extension->config =
